The lead agency in providing this service is Youth Alternatives located at 1328 Talbot Court,
Cheyenne, Wyoming
E.Goals of theprogram:
1.To identify and assess the needs of families who have one or more risk factors in their
lives that increases their potential for out of home placement.
2.To provide early intervention services to families designed to strengthen parenting
skils, improve family interaction and overall functioning enabling high risk youth to
return and/or remain safely at home.
3.Toimprove resiliency in children by providing them with positive alternatives and
enhancing their self-esteem and coping skills.
4.To increase access to services for under-served families thereby, helping them
identify risk factor and the assets needed to maintain a healthy family.
F.Summary of Program:
This project is primarily designed to be a front-end program, however, the services will also
be effective when children are returning from out of home placement.The program utilizes
a variety of best practice approaches tointervene early and provide services that will keep
children safely at home.The primary components are:
