Attn: Wyoming Department of Administration and Information Procurement Section
RE: Letter of Support for Youth Alternatives Family Preservation Grant
Dear Committee Members,
Youth Alternatives is the primary provider of services to troubled youth and families in Cheyenne and Laramie County.
They are a public entity and we strongly believe that the public needs easy access.to the type of services offered by their
agency.
The incarceration and placement of juveniles out of their homes is one of the great tragedies in our community.1
believe that it is extremely important that weimplement programs for our troubled youth that protect the community
and provide preventive and corrective services to juveniles and their families.It is our belief that appropriate early
intervention is the best deterrent to future criminal involvement.Although the community must be protected it is
important to treat juveniles differently from adults.Dealing with juveniles requires a holistic perspective that protects
the community andcorrects the juveniles's behavior.
Laramie County and the City of Cheyenne are very committed to helping our youth.Thisis demonstrated by the over
40 years of support we have provided to Youth Alternatives.Personally we are very strong advocates for mentoring,
counseling, tutoring and other early interventions for children and their families.Like most of us, we have experienced
wonderful role models in our lives.Providing adult role models, positive activities, parent support, etc.will greatly
impact the lives of children in our community.
We believe this is money well spent and we urgeyou to strongly consider this application.Youth Alternatives has a
proven track record of success and this funding will only further there mission to help children and families
Sincerely,
Rick Kaysen
Gay Woodhouse
Mayor, City of Cheyenne
Chairman, Laramie County Commissioners
