Family Preservation RFP NO.0269-V
Letter of Support: Youth Alternatives Grant Proposal
Dear Review Committee Members:
It is with great pleasure I write this letter of support for the proposal submitted by the Office of Youth
Alternatives to provide family preservation services in Cheyenne.I have worked closely with Youth
Alternatives and I feel they are committed to offering quality services tojuveniles and their families.
Our department depends heavily on them as a referral source for juveniles and families.Presently, our
officers encourage contact and distribute information about Youth Alternatives to juveniles who are issued
a citation for a misdemeanor offense.Additionally, before status offense citations, like runaway, are
issued thefamilyis directed to contact Youth Alternatives.
Juvenile offenders are extremely time consuming and difficult for law enforcement to work with.It has
been our experience that when juveniles and their parents have positive role modcls in their lives they are
less involved in delinquent or criminal activity.Providing mentioning and other prevention services to
high risk juveniles and their parents will enhance their ability to resolve personal conflicts and improve
family interactions.This wilincrease the potential for the young people to be successfully diverted from
future involvement in the juvenile justice system.
We currently have three police officers who are participating as mentors with the program.Our Diversion
Officer was previously recognized as the Mentor of the Year for his one-to-one work with youth.I
continue to encourage our officers to get involved in the community and volunteering their time with the
prevention programs for Youth Alternatives not only benefits the young people but it helps develop
positive relationships betveen the police and the youth.
I hope you will give this proposal strong consideration.
Sincerely,
The
Brian Kozak
Chiefof Police
